lse,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0090. The changes meet the goal, stay inside the contract, and fit the budget. The factory had already run the acceptance oracle on this commit, so I didn't rerun it.\n\n**Goal**\n- **color-mods:** The old `IS_APPROX_EQUALS` switch, which only covered R, G and B, is gone. Each case is now one assertion allowing ±1 on R, G, B and A, and a failure message shows the actual and expected colours. That is what the packet asked for. The tolerance applies to one channel's value at a time, not added across channels, so it can't hide a larger error.\n- **chartEx-serialize:** The page now sets `g_fonts_selection_bin = \"\"` before the scripts load, and it loads only the slide scripts. \"Compare 1xml\" is skipped, with the reason given in both the code and the test name.\n- **Surprise:** `CChartSpace` only has generic placeholder serializer methods. The new \"Page boots\" test keeps this behaviour pinned with an `assert.throws` that expects a `TypeError`, through the `OpenXmlPackage.getXmlBytes` path. The comment on the skipped test now matches: only that path throws, and calling `toXml` directly does not. If a real serializer is ever added, this test fails and tells whoever is working on it to re-enable \"Compare 1xml\".\n- **Oracle and Atlas:** The `known` list in `sdkjs-common-run.cjs` is empty, and the shape of its entries is documented for future use. The Atlas card's totals and rows match: chartEx 4/4, everything 10327/10327.\n\n**Contract:** No sdkjs product code changed, only the three test files listed in the target. The four upstream api suites still pass.\n\n**Required records:** The Executor log is filled in and records the surprise and decisions. The follow-up for the stale header comment in `.theseus/oracle/sdkjs-common.sh` is filed in `.theseus/spawn/` and listed under Spawned packets.\n\n**Minor note:** Comparing only R, G, B and A means the colour objects' other fields are no longer checked, unlike the old `deepEqual`. That is acceptable: the goal asked for this comparison, and the expected values are built only from R, G, B and A.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Goal met: ±1 tolerance on R, G, B and A, chartEx boots and the serializer surprise is kept in a test, `known` emptied, Atlas and follow-up recorded","ttft_ms":4473,"type":"result","duration_ms":22846,"uuid":"22a3b4f8-534c-404d-8ddd-3ffb23fb33fc","ttft_stream_ms":3033,"time_to_request_ms":265,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":74,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":20,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":32,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":20,"query_setup":6,"auto_mode_context_wait":8,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":31,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":20,"request_build":15},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":85,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":189,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":180,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":104,"process_rss_mib_result":211,"process_anon_mib_result":122,"process_peak_rss_mib":220,"process_cpu_ms_turn":881,"process_wall_ms_turn":22846,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":297,"process_wall_ms_streaming":12333,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":239,"main_stream_chunk_count":64,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":8,"cpu_ms":19,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":9,"ambient_wait_ms":7,"render_ms":2,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":3038,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":9827974,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793668520395.8909,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"process_start_tuning":0}
